## 1. Definitions

1.1 "We" means the CMI development team and its designated maintainers.
1.2 "The Pack" means the Minecraft modpack Create: Mechanism and Innovation (CMI), including the code, KubeJS scripts, data, configuration, documentation and art assets we publish in this repository, together with the bundled Third-Party Components.
1.3 "Project Content" means the portions of the Pack created by us or lawfully held by us, including but not limited to code, scripts, data, configuration, documentation and art assets, excluding Third-Party Components.
1.4 "Art Assets" means the art assets of the Pack made by us, as defined in LICENSE-ASSETS.
1.5 "Third-Party Components" means content created or licensed by third parties and included in the Pack, including but not limited to third-party mods, third-party resource packs, Minecraft vanilla assets, and third-party audio and fonts.
1.6 "Distribute" means providing the Pack or any copy of it to others by any means, including but not limited to downloads, transfers, mirrors, cloud sharing and packaged releases.
1.7 "This Agreement" means this document together with LICENSE-ASSETS and the respective licenses of the Third-Party Components.

## 2. Acceptance

2.1 By downloading, installing, running or distributing the Pack, you confirm that you have read, understood and agree to be bound by this Agreement.
2.2 If you do not agree to all of its terms, you must immediately stop using the Pack and delete all copies.
2.3 If you use the Pack on behalf of an organization, you represent that you are authorized to do so.

## 3. Grant of License

Subject to this Agreement, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable and revocable license to:
(a) download, install and run the Pack on your personal devices (including on a private, non-profit server you operate yourself) for personal entertainment;
(b) modify configuration files, scripts and local settings for personal use;
(c) redistribute the Pack to others free of charge in accordance with Section 5.

All rights not expressly granted are reserved by us.

## 4. Restrictions

4.1 No Commercial Distribution. You may not charge any fee for redistributing the Pack or any Project Content, including but not limited to:
(a) selling the Pack or any paid product containing it;
(b) placing the Pack behind a paywall, membership, subscription or paid download;
(c) using the Pack as a primary selling point of a paid product or service where the substance of the paid service is providing downloads or installation of the Pack;
(d) charging indirectly by limiting download speed, download count or access.

This Section governs your distribution of the Pack and its Project Content; Third-Party Components are governed by their own licenses. Videos, livestreams, articles and similar works you create featuring the Pack are not restricted by this Section, provided that you do not use them to circumvent the fee restriction on distribution itself.

4.2 You may not remove, obscure or modify copyright notices, license files (LICENSE, LICENSE-ASSETS) or the links they contain.

4.3 You may not claim to be the developer or an official publisher of the Pack, or distribute or promote it under the names CMI or Create: Mechanism and Innovation (see Section 6).

4.4 You may not use the Pack or Project Content for purposes that violate the laws of the People's Republic of China or the laws applicable to you.

4.5 You may not circumvent this Agreement by technical means, including removing license files or splitting Project Content for distribution under another name.

4.6 Except as expressly granted by Section 5 of this Agreement or LICENSE-ASSETS, you may not copy, modify, translate, compile, reverse engineer or create derivative works of Project Content.

## 5. Redistribution and Open-Source Requirement

5.1 You may redistribute the Pack free of charge for non-commercial purposes, provided that you:
(a) retain all copyright notices and the complete, unmodified texts of this Agreement and LICENSE-ASSETS;
(b) clearly attribute the source: Create: Mechanism and Innovation (CMI) and the project URL;
(c) clearly mark any modifications, the modifier and the date of modification;
(d) do not charge any fee (see Section 4.1);
(e) ensure that recipients are bound by this Agreement.

5.2 Open-Source Requirement. If you use the Project Content's code or resource files (in whole or in substantial part) to create a derivative project or to republish, your project must be open source: the source code must be publicly visible and permit redistribution and modification by others. For the purposes of this Agreement, "open source" means source availability and permission to redistribute and modify; it does not permit commercial distribution. This requirement does not apply to use of Art Assets solely under LICENSE-ASSETS, which is governed by CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

5.3 Any redistribution beyond Sections 5.1 and 5.2, including commercial distribution, requires our prior written permission under Section 10.

## 6. Intellectual Property

6.1 Copyright and other intellectual property rights in the Project Content belong to us or the respective contributors.
6.2 The Art Assets are additionally licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 as set out in LICENSE-ASSETS, in parallel with this Agreement. This Agreement does not reduce your rights under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, but commercial use remains restricted by Section 4.1.
6.3 Third-Party Components belong to their respective owners and are not governed by this Agreement; their use, copying and distribution are subject to their own licenses.
6.4 No trademark, trade name or logo rights are granted. Without prior written permission, you may not use the names CMI or Create: Mechanism and Innovation, or the icon (icon.png), as the name or identifier of your project, product or service in a way that may cause confusion as to official association with the Project. Copying of Art Assets under LICENSE-ASSETS remains subject to the attribution requirements of CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
6.5 All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

## 7. Contributions

7.1 By submitting a contribution to the Project, you agree to license it to the Project on the same terms as Sections 3, 4 and 5, and you represent that you are entitled to grant that license.
7.2 Contributions of code and resources are subject to the open-source requirement in Section 5.2.

